'''Android 16''' is the [[Android version history|sixteenth major release]] and the 23rd version of [[Android (operating system)|Android]], the mobile operating system developed by the [[Open Handset Alliance]] and led by [[Google]]. The first developer preview was released on November 19, 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Weatherbed |first=Jess |date=2024-11-19 |title=Android 16 is now available for early testers |url=https://www.theverge.com/2024/11/19/24300673/android-16-developer-preview-availability-release-timeline |access-date=2024-11-20 |website=The Verge |language=en |archive-date=November 19, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241119190426/https://www.theverge.com/2024/11/19/24300673/android-16-developer-preview-availability-release-timeline |url-status=live }}</ref> The first beta was released on January 23, 2025.<ref name=":2">{{Cite web |title=The First Beta of Android 16 |url=https://android-developers.googleblog.com/2025/01/first-beta-android16.html |access-date=2025-01-24 |website=Android Developers Blog |language=en |archive-date=January 24, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250124035557/https://android-developers.googleblog.com/2025/01/first-beta-android16.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Google released the final version on June 10, 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-06-10 |title=Android 16 is out, complete with live notification updates and new camera features |url=https://www.engadget.com/mobile/android-16-is-out-complete-with-live-notification-updates-and-new-camera-features-170006072.html |access-date=2025-06-10 |website=Engadget |language=en-US |archive-date=June 10, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250610180151/https://www.engadget.com/mobile/android-16-is-out-complete-with-live-notification-updates-and-new-camera-features-170006072.html |url-status=live }}</ref> The first devices to ship with Android 16 are the [[Samsung Galaxy Z Fold 7]], [[Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 7|Galaxy Z Flip 7]], and its [[Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 7 FE|FE]] model.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Shaik |first=Asif Iqbal |date=2025-04-05 |title=Exclusive: Samsung’s Galaxy Z Fold 7, Flip 7 will launch with One UI 8 onboard |url=https://www.sammobile.com/news/samsung-galaxy-z-fold-7-flip-7-one-ui-8-preloaded/ |access-date=2026-08-07 |website=SamMobile |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mishra |first=Abhijeet |date=2025-05-28 |title=Galaxy Z Fold 7 and Flip 7 confirmed to launch with One UI 8 preloaded |url=https://www.sammobile.com/news/samsung-galaxy-z-fold-7-flip-7-one-ui-8-android-16/ |access-date=2026-08-07 |website=SamMobile |language=en-US}}</ref>

{{As of|2026|07}}, 25.49% of Android devices run Android 16, making it the most widely used version of Android.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Mobile and Tablet Android version Market Share Worldwide |url=https://gs.statcounter.com/android-version-market-share/ |access-date=2026-08-01|website=StatCounter Global Stats |language=en}}</ref>
